Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond, Humanity's Last Exam, FrontierMath Tier 4, ARC-AGI-3, HealthBench: OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra evaluation rows — again the prior confirmed ID.

Coding:

- Terminal-Bench 4.0, DeepSWE, FrontierCode: GPT-6 Astra launch-post coding tables — prior confirmed ID.

Long context:

- OpenAI MRCR v2 long-context retrieval rows: GPT-6 Astra — prior confirmed ID.

### Cross-source comparison

- Official OpenAI sources (GPT-6 Astra launch post + system card, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Sol/Luna, GPT-6-Cyber, safety overview): contain no GPT-6.2 material; OpenAI's newsroom, API changelog and API models listings were checked and show no GPT-6.2 entry as of 2026-11-13.
- Independent coverage (TestingCatalog Codex usage-analytics report, geotoolbox.ai GPT-6.2 synthesis, EvoLink GPT-6.2 release watch, The Information, Sam Altman ADIPEC remarks, Google Cloud console quota screenshots): all describe sightings, rumors, demos and expectations — none yield a standardized, independently reproducible public benchmark number for the GPT-6.2 Astra identity.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- SELF-EXCLUSION: zero verified public benchmark numbers found for the GPT-6.2 Astra subject identity (`openai/gpt-6.2-astra` / `openai/gpt-6.2-sol`) in independently accessible public sources as of 2026-11-13; OpenAI has not announced GPT-6.2 and published no context window, pricing or benchmark for it, and every measured benchmark figure retrieved in accessible sources belongs to the prior confirmed GPT-6 Astra / GPT-6.1 Sol IDs; no scored file written and no dimension scores assigned.

